hostname r2
!
ip routing
!
interface Loopback0
   ip address 10.0.0.2/32
!
interface Ethernet1
   description to r1:eth1
   no switchport
   ip address 10.1.12.2/30
!
interface Ethernet2
   description to r3:eth1
   no switchport
   ip address 10.1.23.1/30
!
! ============================================================
! YOUR TASKS ON R2
! ============================================================
!
! TASK 1 — Base BGP session
!   configure
!   router bgp 65002
!      bgp router-id 10.0.0.2
!      neighbor 10.1.12.1 remote-as 65001
!      neighbor 10.1.23.2 remote-as 65003
!      !
!      address-family ipv4
!         neighbor 10.1.12.1 activate
!         neighbor 10.1.23.2 activate
!         network 10.0.0.2/32
!      !
!
! TASK 2 — Match community 65001:100 and set local-preference
!   When r1 tags its prefix with 65001:100, r2 can act on it.
!   Higher local-pref = preferred path.
!
!   ip community-list standard PREF-COMM permit 65001:100
!
!   route-map MATCH-COMM permit 10
!      match community PREF-COMM
!      set local-preference 200
!   route-map MATCH-COMM permit 20
!      ! permit everything else with default local-pref
!
!   Apply inbound from r1:
!   router bgp 65002
!      address-family ipv4
!         neighbor 10.1.12.1 route-map MATCH-COMM in
!      !
!
!   Verify: show bgp ipv4 unicast 10.0.0.1/32
!   Look for "Local Pref: 200" (or similar field) in the output.
!
! TASK 3 — Filter (deny) based on community
!   Instead of adjusting local-pref, drop the route entirely:
!
!   route-map BLOCK-COMM deny 10
!      match community PREF-COMM
!   route-map BLOCK-COMM permit 20
!
!   router bgp 65002
!      address-family ipv4
!         neighbor 10.1.12.1 route-map BLOCK-COMM in
!      !
!
!   After applying (clear bgp * soft-inbound), 10.0.0.1/32 disappears from r2's table.
!
! TASK 4 — Stripping communities before forwarding
!   You may want to accept a route but strip the community before
!   sending it on to r3, so r3 doesn't see it:
!
!   route-map STRIP-COMM permit 10
!      set community none
!
!   router bgp 65002
!      address-family ipv4
!         neighbor 10.1.23.2 route-map STRIP-COMM out
!      !
!
! NOTE: After changing route-map or community-list, apply with:
!   clear bgp * soft-inbound    ! re-evaluate inbound policy
!   clear bgp * soft-outbound   ! re-advertise with new outbound policy
! ============================================================
end
